think Built image/font5x7_greek_upper.rye -- Gamma, Theta, Lambda, Xi, Pi, Phi, Psi (U+0393,U+0398,U+039B,U+039E,U+03A0,U+03A6,U+03A8), the seven that carry a shape of their own; the rest of the Greek uppercase alphabet is a Latin twin (Alpha=A, Rho=P, Chi=X) spelled from the ASCII font already loaded. Modeled exactly on the family: art-is-spec ASCII line drawings, coverage lifted from the art, gfa1 round-trip, present/distinct/legible band, and each construction read by its OWN toothed guard.
think Chose seven distinguishing guards rather than a shared placement check: Gamma's bar over a lone left stem with NO right leg (tells it from Pi), Theta's crossed oval with rounded top corners (tells it from a square-topped bar), Lambda's apex with an open foot (tells it from Psi's stem), Xi's blank row below the top bar (no stem, tells it from Pi), Pi's two legs with an open center, Phi's stem poking above and below a crossed bowl, Psi's three top prongs gathering to a bottom stem.
